# fuzz_server_messages: the first byte picks the message (0 registration request,
# 1 record, 2 KE1, 3 KE3). The registration request, the KE1 and the record are
# made of ristretto255 points (32 bytes); the record ends in a masking key, a
# nonce and a MAC. KE3 is one 64 byte MAC. The profile of a record is claimed
# in the first four bytes after the select byte.
